#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048703 :topic/difficulty 1.032628248382348 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429644 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 831->203. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048867} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "b6736188-d97d-5582-895d-df6495a8ef81" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087669 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087477 :question/id #uuid "7826cd52-8603-51ff-902e-c7764639dccd" :question/math-academy-id "e-3666" :question/problem "Express $$\n\\displaystyle \\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)} - \\sin^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\n$$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\cos }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)-{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087670 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087478 :question/id #uuid "2b9dc462-ec26-5762-aa64-d9e8f16112c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3667" :question/problem "Express $2\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2 \\cos^2 x - 1 = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\cos }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff17ae-9319-5498-a5e0-1d49ddbef50a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087671 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087479 :question/id #uuid "e617aaf2-1232-57cc-8644-2467effda030" :question/math-academy-id "e-3668" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\cos^2\\left( 22.5^\\circ\\right) - \\sin^2\\left( 22.5^\\circ\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={22.5^\\circ}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\cos }^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘})-{\\sin }^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {22.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :topic/math-academy-id 831 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048211} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048307} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049144} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049303} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049835} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050031} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050660}] :topic/title "The Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}]}
